  "contracts": {
    "prompt": "Exact plain bytes, exactly six bytes; packed 01D4 distinguished from equally sized numeric 0142 and unknowns; zero rejected conservatively, not universal script-OID claim.",
    "id": "Plain int 1..FFFFFFFF preserved bit-for-bit; signed outgoing int32 interpretation can be negative, not valid-NPC authorization.",
    "name": "Exact plain str encoded strict UTF-8, 1..23 bytes; preserves case, spaces and composed/decomposed forms without normalization, coercion or truncation; empty/NUL/surrogate/overflow rejected. This is selected-name policy, not arbitrary NPC input support or universal charset/name legality.",
    "response": "01D5, packed eight-byte prefix, declared size=8+N, no wire terminal NUL. Active PACKETVER>=20151001 increments N to N+1; actual safestrncpy sets destination[--n]=0 and loops over at most N source bytes. N<=23 below CHATBOX_SIZE71, so no source read beyond payload and exact destination bytes followed by NUL. Source review plus independent Python emulation only, not actual C++ execution.",
    "types": "Ordinary subclasses/overridden comparison, encode and length hooks rejected before execution; hostile object.__setattr__ mutation of frozen records is outside this ordinary API contract.",
    "boundaries": "No actor lookup, hidden world flags, context/name selection, stream collector registration, continuity/epoch binding, ownership, permissions, gameplay, spending or rewards."
  },
